[{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-23T01:01:50Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"21c9f56990197d81b18529c8d4f069f8ab88294c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-22T06:00:20Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"b9adec5c7cd52c47c510c939f3ed4c18d554abd1"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-22T05:00:25Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(license): relicense project under CC0-1.0\n\n- Replaced Land Public License v1.0 with Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal\n  to dedicate work to public domain, removing copyleft requirements\n- Updated Element submodule reference (likely aligning with license change)\n- Excluded build artifacts from version control (Target/debug & Target/release)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: This changes legal terms from copyleft to public domain dedication.\nAll previous licensing obligations under LPL-1.0 are revoked in favor of\nunrestricted use under CC0-1.0. Contributors must acknowledge new license terms.","SHA":"ab89eed343ffb6567e925dfba2a99ec2b329df54"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-22T03:13:26Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"s\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"7f9733ee59a953fe4b8806c645043ab2546aadb0"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-22T01:01:56Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"c50a1345bb26071363132ba65b8ddf9138e3a3b5"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-21T06:00:19Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"a8e054f0dead8865a9a199973289cb33c44a1620"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-21T05:27:28Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(Element): Update submodule reference to latest commit\n\n- Updates Element submodule from 330653f to 482b3ff to incorporate recent changes from the upstream repository\n- Ensures Land project remains synchronized with latest component developments in Element directory\n- May include updates to various Element components (Grove, Mist, Rest, Wind etc.) that could affect:\n  - Extension host shim behavior (Cocoon)\n  - Native FS operations (River/Sun)\n  - UI component library (Wind)\n  - Build toolchain configuration (Rest)\n- Maintains compatibility with evolving Element subcomponents critical for Land's VS Code migration goals","SHA":"d6aa1703ad21073f90c5f5727f5abcae5d83f808"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-21T05:19:05Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"build(Release): Include release binaries for Mountain backend\n\n- Adds compiled Mountain.exe (8.4MB) as core Tauri/Rust backend executable\n- Packages Windows MSI (6.6MB) and NSIS (5.8MB) installers for distribution\n- Marks first official release binaries meeting Land's MVP performance goals\n\nThese artifacts represent the first complete build of the Mountain component following Tauri migration, enabling:\n- Native Windows installation via standard package formats\n- Validation of binary size reductions compared to Electron baseline\n- Foundation for upcoming end-to-end testing of Sky/Cocoon integration\n\nRefs #123 (Release pipeline implementation)","SHA":"89105ca81741d242dc76f2795ea26abc217bdaa7"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-21T03:37:49Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"19ac4f82105468c1c95813903cf9a1aa70e2a4e9"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-21T03:36:50Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): Update distribution artifacts for Mountain backend\n\n- Regenerated debug/release executables and installers for Mountain (Tauri backend)\n- Includes NSIS (Windows) and MSI installer packages for both build configurations\n- Artifact size reductions observed in release builds (e.g. main EXE: 39MB debug vs 8.3MB release)\n\nThese binaries represent the compiled Mountain backend component following recent changes to the Tauri configuration and build process. As part of Land's Electron-to-Tauri migration strategy, maintaining lean build artifacts is critical for achieving the project's performance goals compared to Electron's larger footprint. The package artifacts will be used for internal testing of the native integration layer before wider distribution.","SHA":"29d521e2e2f4dad22602977c569ed8db7d1f17d8"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-21T01:02:27Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"679c70cef624919d54171b912df3f1c47ecbb886"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-20T21:39:24Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"a14db1d62fd48df7f91959957eb927379e6f0022"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-20T18:38:02Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"e811e8efc353103d5eb9471a9437ec4041205de1"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-20T18:37:26Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): Standardize URLs and exclude build artifacts\n\n- Corrected HTTPS URLs to lowercase in documentation (CODE_OF_CONDUCT, CONTRIBUTING), configuration (.npmrc, Cargo.toml), and package.json for consistency.\n- Reformatted README.md table structure to improve readability while maintaining badge functionality.\n- Updated Element submodule reference to latest commit (330653f).\n- Added .gitignore exclusions for build artifacts in Target/debug and Target/release directories to prevent accidental versioning of binaries.\n\nEnsures proper URL casing for compatibility across systems, maintains clean repository state by excluding build outputs, and keeps submodule dependencies current.","SHA":"9a2712be2b2236c31c5127802f3f32ef3b546c2a"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-20T01:02:59Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"36fedf6a7542f1fb9134b272023150d5263c3603"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-19T01:04:58Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"a187f6681b36df0a0e1adf37764ef392eb8084a2"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T12:01:21Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"d58672c9d90648408d39d6fe64d9864d013bd84c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T10:29:21Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"docs(README): Expand with detailed architecture and roadmap\n\n- Completely restructured README to reflect Land's phased development strategy (MVP Path A/B)\n- Added comprehensive explanations of core components: Mountain (Tauri backend), Sky (UI), Cocoon (Node.js sidecar), Vine (IPC)\n- Documented future extension host paths: Grove (Rust/WASM) and alternative runtimes (Deno/LLRT)\n- Included detailed build process instructions with environment variable explanations\n- Added system architecture diagrams (Mermaid) for MVP Path A and build-time processes\n- Clarified project structure with component mapping to directories\n- Outlined funding sources and acknowledgements section\n\nThis update provides critical context for contributors, aligning documentation with current implementation (Cocoon-based extension hosting) while establishing vision for native Rust/WASM future. Enables better onboarding by explaining component interactions and long-term goals.","SHA":"11638d2b378c4d1d9e6808c363b8f54181c93fec"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:29:52Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"5e2424605ce1eb00e7d2778e95ab53c9891db655"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:27:47Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"ebb13f40351873fa05422e57eae93a973605c43c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:26:05Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"86051f7290aa37c15011dba69e8ebb530fcb207b"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:24:25Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"53d8920431f8955ad8dad2030e3ee33f72ce679f"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:20:02Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"9c0b077ca351e7ac2e202a2eeb9b8492f24e3f41"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-18T03:19:31Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): update dev dependencies to latest patch versions\n\n- Updated multiple Prettier plugins (autocorrect, packagejson, sh, sql, svelte, toml) to their latest patch versions to ensure consistent code formatting across Sky frontend and Cocoon extension shim\n- Upgraded @vue/compiler-sfc to 3.5.14 to maintain compatibility with Vue template processing in Astro components\n- Bumped prettier-plugin-pkg and related formatters to improve package.json validation during build process\n\nThese updates help maintain security fixes and stability in Land's development toolchain while preserving VS Code UI migration efforts. Dependency hygiene ensures reliable builds for both Tauri backend and webview frontend components.","SHA":"236890cdfa72d063f9a983c4657ce96a4c060a57"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-18T01:06:13Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"c1cbeb8aa0f02602ef82d4a78e44cf72b53c8fd7"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-17T01:00:54Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",100,1],"Message":"","SHA":"cd42319d33de3e17d843d2b200a05ce2329fdd0b"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-16T01:02:21Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",100,1],"Message":"","SHA":"1d233ad67c40d9b94d9a429f4eb2b51d34b73d5e"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-15T18:18:56Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",100,5],"Message":"build(Release): Update release artifacts and submodule dependencies\n\n- Updated Dependency and Element submodules to latest commits, ensuring alignment with upstream improvements in core components\n- Regenerated Mountain.exe binary and platform-specific installer packages (MSI/NSIS) as part of release build process\n\nThese changes reflect successful compilation of the Tauri-based Mountain backend with updated dependencies, critical for:\n- Validating the cross-platform build pipeline\n- Incorporating latest fixes/features from submodules that may address MVP requirements\n- Preparing distributable packages for initial performance testing against Electron baseline\n\nMaintains progress toward Land's primary objective of delivering a production-ready native code editor with minimized resource footprint.","SHA":"93be38