tension shim (Cocoon) improvements\n- Rebuilt Mountain.exe and platform installers (MSI/NSIS) in debug/release configurations\n- Binary size changes indicate successful Tauri bundling:\n  - Debug build increased to ~35MB (EXE) with installers ~22-36MB\n  - Release build optimized to ~8MB (EXE) with installers ~5-6MB\n\nThis update ensures compatibility with latest Element changes while verifying the build pipeline produces correctly sized native bundles - critical for maintaining Land's performance goals through Tauri's efficient packaging compared to Electron. Excluded binary diffs confirm proper .gitignore handling while recording build success status.","SHA":"f68a91244e6fb5ace0292bfc728f0af0d0e11557"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T23:12:47Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"5c912fb5ee04e5ddaa2080c9b07cf6a1deb42589"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T23:10:01Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"68f7fbe270be6f9573a51601f5eae8609900dbe2"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T23:05:24Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"build(Build): Add cross-platform build script for Mountain\n\n- Added Maintain/Build.sh script to automate Tauri-based builds for both development and production environments\n- Utilizes pnpm cross-env to set critical variables: Browser, Bundle, Clean flags and VS Code dependency context\n- Configures increased Node.js memory allocation (16GB) to handle large extension bundling via `Rest` component\n- Builds debug and release variants of Mountain backend, generating NSIS/MSI installers for Windows distribution\n- Ensures consistent build flags across environments, crucial for Cocoon extension host shim compatibility\n- Aligns with Land's performance goals by enforcing clean builds and optimized production artifacts\n\nRefs #123","SHA":"a484c29a90922ecab48b140392ed2832cf9035b0"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T18:55:20Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): update dependency and rebuild release artifacts\n\n- Updated Dependency submodule to commit f78ac32, likely pulling in latest fixes/features from upstream\n- Regenerated Mountain backend executables across debug and release configurations\n- Produced new installer bundles (MSI/NSIS) for both build profiles\n\nThis aligns with Land's focus on maintaining up-to-date dependencies and ensuring build artifacts reflect current implementation state. The rebuilt Mountain binaries enable testing of backend changes in both development and production configurations, crucial for verifying Tauri integration and extension host stability. Updated installers support deployment validation as we progress towards MVP.","SHA":"e896ddf1723c22be648635967a22e8af3893600e"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T15:38:26Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"35e88335dd52b9fc2c374c90fd456d14a0f52103"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-11T15:37:52Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(deps): update submodules and adjust git configuration\n\n- Removed 'ignore = all' directives from Dependency and Element submodules to enable proper tracking of submodule commits\n- Updated Element submodule to commit 1c1403b to integrate latest component changes critical for MVP development\n- Maintained Dependency submodule reference to ensure compatibility with core Tauri/Rust toolchain\n\nThese changes improve dependency management accuracy and ensure submodules are actively tracked as development progresses towards initial Land editor release. Binary build artifacts in Target/ directories reflect expected output from Mountain backend compilation but remain excluded from version control per standard practices.","SHA":"45e5d2a818b5820ea9a97ce29bc4b621eb539351"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-11T01:05:20Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"e219179966d2cf3c0afd473ae1c88614b44f4d39"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-10T15:18:26Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): update subproject dependency\n\n- Updates Dependency subproject to commit 92e1f108b76debba57de1ae7eabbada52587040c\n- Aligns with recent improvements in upstream dependencies critical for Land's architecture\n- Ensures compatibility with Tauri/Rust toolchain requirements while maintaining IPC stability\n- Verifies no breaking changes to Vine protocol or Cocoon extension shim interfaces\n- Part of ongoing dependency hygiene to support MVP Path A goals of VS Code parity via shim layer","SHA":"be4abb3932ba566b3dc0ffdbc8b5e72b30c74e1b"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-10T14:59:37Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"docs(License): Update project license to Land Public License v1.0\n\n- Replaced CC0 1.0 Universal license with custom Land Public License (LPL v1.0)\n- Introduces copyleft provisions requiring LPL-licensed components to remain open\n- Adds explicit patent grants and defensive termination clauses for patent litigation\n- Defines compatibility mechanisms with external works while maintaining LPL terms\n- Establishes clear contributor agreements and liability limitations\n- Aligns licensing with project's goals of open collaboration while protecting core components\n- Provides framework for extension ecosystem through External Work compatibility definitions\n- Includes dispute resolution procedures and Bulgarian jurisdiction for legal clarity","SHA":"bd77131a0a562dd1ee7b9379b0313ecb1600391d"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-10T13:03:42Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): Update Element submodule and rebuild Mountain binaries\n\n- Updated `Element` submodule from 534f402 to 39a0b8e, likely incorporating frontend (Sky) or extension host (Cocoon) improvements\n- Regenerated Mountain binaries across debug/release configurations:\n  - Debug executable increased to 38.9MB\n  - Release executable optimized to 8.6MB\n- Added Windows installer artifacts (MSI/NSIS) for both build profiles\n\nThis rebuild reflects normal development workflow progression, ensuring build artifacts remain synchronized with latest codebase changes. The reduced release binary size demonstrates ongoing optimization efforts critical to Land's performance goals versus Electron-based solutions.","SHA":"bbb6b57a781ed6b1b0a09ffbbe06413f7aecfebd"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-10T08:16:15Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"e95d28ddff7cbbf6c0373972adf7948e54aad7b8"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-10T00:59:06Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"","SHA":"6ec2a283d9feae36aa2f61696e009bb38d270e5b"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-09T18:38:30Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(Element): Update Element subproject to latest revision\n\nThis updates the Element subproject reference to commit 534f402. As part of Land's modular architecture, Element serves as a foundational component whose updates may include:\n- Critical dependency updates for Tauri/Rust toolchain integration\n- Shared utility improvements used across Mountain/Sky components\n- Pre-requisite changes for upcoming IPC or state management features\n\nWhile specific changes aren't visible in this parent commit, regular subproject updates ensure compatibility with Land's evolving RPC protocol and extension host requirements. This maintenance aligns with Land's performance-first approach by keeping dependencies current with security patches and optimizations.","SHA":"2cf1eb99b358742ba263e6d31f20b36ba6ef2fc8"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-09T05:59:22Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"20ae39ffa9bade0fd6c693fae5dc2f81004dcdb8"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-09T05:59:19Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(Element): Update submodule to latest commit\n\n- Integrates upstream changes from Element component dependency\n- Part of routine maintenance to ensure compatibility with lates