and project components. This update likely includes improvements to shared infrastructure elements (Grove, Mist, Rest, Wind, or Worker) that support the core MVP architecture.\n\nWhile specific diff details aren't visible in submodule updates, such maintenance ensures:\n- Compatibility with recent protocol changes in Vine IPC layer\n- Updated shim implementations in Cocoon extension host\n- Enhanced FS abstraction through River/Sun libraries\n- Preparation for upcoming WASM runtime integration in Grove\n\nRegular subproject updates help maintain development velocity as we progress toward VS Code parity in the Tauri-based architecture.","SHA":"60ee3da627d106613fb252a23676f34c3e07d9df"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-06T11:03:20Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"build(Build): add production build configuration flags\n\n- Added Browser, Bundle, Clean flags to control build pipeline steps\n- Set Dependency=Microsoft/VSCode to align with upstream code dependencies\n- Configured NODE_ENV=production for optimized build output\n- Increased NODE_OPTIONS memory limit to 16GB for resource-intensive bundling\n- Maintained TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY placeholder for future signing\n\nchore(deps): update Element submodule to latest commit\n\n- Updates Element component (containing Mountain/Sky/Cocoon implementations) to b675cd1\n- Includes latest changes from core architecture components needed for production build","SHA":"42789de0516966f7f45f519c537bbd597925ee75"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-06T06:03:43Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",0,0],"Message":"chore(build): update Dependency and Element submodules to latest commits\n\n- Updates `Dependency` submodule to commit 84d0b0c, aligning with required changes in the JS bundler configuration (Rest component) for Cocoon's extension host environment\n- Updates `Element` submodule to commit 6d0dbc2, incorporating recent improvements to the IPC protocol (Vine layer) and extension shim APIs (Cocoon/Shim)\n\nThese updates ensur